  "difficulty_reason": "The proof identifies the weighted core-size lattice statistic as a degree n+2 quasipolynomial, uses shifted-alcove Ehrhart reciprocity to force all n exponent roots of its enumerator, and then determines the remaining leading factor by explicit hand calculation on the threefold dilated alcove, in type B and again independently in type C. This combines a nontrivial quasipolynomial/Ehrhart mechanism with two complete case computations and assembles them into one uniform expectation identity, above ordinary qualification exercises in affine Weyl groups and Ehrhart theory.",
